{"ts": 1784363391.8772457, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held throughout \u2014 this SHORT entry was correct-direction the whole way. It dipped several times into a -4 to -12 chop band in the first ~20 minutes (never a clean directional breakdown, ER10 stayed near-zero during those dips signaling noise not trend), then built a sustained favorable move from minute 22 onward, closing near +39.5pts favorable at the frame-window limit with no EXIT triggered. What told me the thesis was intact: repeated recovery back toward/through breakeven after each dip, ER10 rising into the 0.4-0.9 range only during the favorable runs (real trend), and lambda_hat_1m staying negative during dips (supporting mean-reversion back toward the entry thesis) rather than flipping and accelerating away. What I'd watch next time: giveback% alone was a noisy trigger (spiked to 60-120% multiple times on small-amplitude legs without meaning anything) \u2014 I'd weight it much less than the combination of ER10 direction and whether a new leg low undercuts the prior leg low with rising ER10, which would be the real breakdown signature I never actually saw here.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 46}
